1
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:18,270
♪I stretch and yawn
when the sun is high in the sky♪

2
00:00:19,170 --> 00:00:23,030
♪A cup of tea and a little tune,
what a carefree life♪

3
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:28,480
♪The fortune teller said
love would come my way this year♪

4
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:32,580
♪But all I see is my food
arriving right on time♪

5
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:35,670
♪No rush, no worries♪

6
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:38,360
♪Love is all a matter of chance♪

7
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,480
♪Flowers bloom and fade♪

8
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,380
♪I'd rather take good care
of myself first♪

9
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:45,580
♪Two orioles sing among
the green willows♪

10
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,970
♪And I still don't have a boyfriend♪

11
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:50,590
♪My best years are nothing
to worry about♪

12
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:53,240
♪I'll stay happily single
till I'm old and gray♪

13
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:07,540
=Besties' Coming Fortune=

14
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:09,980
=Episode 14=

15
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:16,420
(Shen Manor)

16
00:01:16,430 --> 00:01:18,230
My poor daughter.

17
00:01:18,790 --> 00:01:20,310
(The Powerful Go Unpunished)
She was murdered,

18
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:22,510
and I couldn't even keep
her body intact.

19
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,680
That good-for-nothing Third Young Master

20
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:27,720
burned her remains to ashes!

21
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:30,060
(Shen Manor)

22
00:01:37,070 --> 00:01:38,030
That's him!

23
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:40,400
He started a fire
in the mortuary last night

24
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:43,200
and burned my daughter's body!

25
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:44,560
The Third Young Master
of the Marquis's Manor

26
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:45,670
certainly lives up to his reputation.

27
00:01:46,870 --> 00:01:47,710
If my mother hadn't

28
00:01:47,710 --> 00:01:49,080
gone to the mortuary
to burn offerings last night

29
00:01:49,430 --> 00:01:50,670
and caught you coming out,

30
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:51,130
(My Poor Daughter)

31
00:01:51,130 --> 00:01:52,170
(Third Young Master Sets Fire)
who would have thought

32
00:01:52,170 --> 00:01:53,540
the Third Young Master
of the Marquis's Manor

33
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:54,580
(Playboy Burns Corpse)
could commit such a heartless act

34
00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:56,200
(Commoners Denied Justice)
as burning a dead woman's body?

35
00:01:58,350 --> 00:02:00,030
My poor daughter

36
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:02,230
can't even rest in peace!

37
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:05,760
The Third Young Master has gone too far!

38
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,720
Are we common folk

39
00:02:07,950 --> 00:02:10,760
supposed to put up with such abuse?

40
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:11,910
I heard

41
00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:12,840
he's a spoiled troublemaker.

42
00:02:12,910 --> 00:02:14,390
It's bad enough
that he never does anything useful.

43
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:15,670
Now he won't even spare the dead!

44
00:02:16,310 --> 00:02:16,760
Disgusting!

45
00:02:16,870 --> 00:02:17,390
Sick!

46
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,700
The old Marquis died too soon.

47
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:22,700
There's no one left to keep him in line.

48
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:23,390
Seriously!

49
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:24,790
What kind of people
are they raising in that manor?

50
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:30,060
(Shen Manor)

51
00:02:30,630 --> 00:02:31,390
He,

52
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,880
in front of everyone,

53
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:35,550
you must explain

54
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:37,360
exactly what happened
at the mortuary last night

55
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:40,110
and what you had to do with it.

56
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:44,110
Grandmother,

57
00:02:45,470 --> 00:02:46,320
I did

58
00:02:46,470 --> 00:02:47,710
go to

59
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:48,670
the mortuary last night.

60
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:49,880
But I certainly didn't

61
00:02:50,630 --> 00:02:51,600
set fire to destroy the body.

62
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:53,110
I was there

63
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:55,420
to perform a postmortem examination.

64
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:56,440
Who are you trying to fool?

65
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:58,390
I wanted to find out the true cause

66
00:02:58,930 --> 00:03:00,020
of this young woman's death.

67
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:00,950
A postmortem examination?

68
00:03:01,430 --> 00:03:03,040
You're a notorious
playboy in the capital.

69
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:04,460
All you do is indulge
in cockfighting and dog racing,

70
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:05,710
eat, drink, and fool around.

71
00:03:05,910 --> 00:03:07,030
And you expect us
to believe you can examine a body?

72
00:03:07,190 --> 00:03:08,590
Who would believe that?

73
00:03:08,590 --> 00:03:09,670
Even common folk like us

74
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,110
wouldn't take up a coroner's work.

75
00:03:11,470 --> 00:03:12,680
Why would a young master
from the Marquis's Manor

76
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:13,310
do such a thing?

77
00:03:13,310 --> 00:03:14,040
I think you

78
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:16,710
were just using
my daughter's body for amusement.

79
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,320
When you were caught,

80
00:03:18,590 --> 00:03:20,590
you tried to destroy the evidence.

81
00:03:20,590 --> 00:03:22,120
These nobles will do anything for fun.

82
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:22,830
Exactly.

83
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,680
We pay them taxes while we're alive,

84
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,080
and even in death,
our bodies become their playthings.

85
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:27,640
I only wanted to uncover the truth

86
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:29,710
and get justice for the deceased.

87
00:03:30,870 --> 00:03:32,640
Why won't any of you believe me?

88
00:03:33,430 --> 00:03:34,390
Now's the time.

89
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:35,710
- I believe...
- I believe you.

90
00:03:43,150 --> 00:03:44,950
You say he set fire to the body.

91
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:45,955
(Shen Manor)
Then why didn't he flee

92
00:03:45,955 --> 00:03:46,790
(Shen Manor)
after setting the fire?

93
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:48,840
And why did he rush into the flames

94
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:49,950
to rescue

95
00:03:50,190 --> 00:03:51,710
a woman's body
that was already badly burned?

96
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:53,670
That makes sense.

97
00:03:54,650 --> 00:03:55,650
They must have mistaken him
for someone else.

98
00:04:00,030 --> 00:04:00,910
Everyone, look.

99
00:04:00,910 --> 00:04:01,760
What's this?

100
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:04,880
The burns on his arm

101
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,320
came from rushing into the flames

102
00:04:06,430 --> 00:04:08,200
to protect your daughter's body.

103
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:09,240
If he really were

104
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:10,360
such a heartless man,

105
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:11,470
why would he

106
00:04:11,470 --> 00:04:12,360
risk saving a dead body

107
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:13,830
and suffer burns like these?

108
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:14,960
What really happened, then?

109
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:15,520
She has a point.

110
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:16,680
Did we accuse him wrongly?

111
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:23,030
Everyone,

112
00:04:23,460 --> 00:04:25,270
- the Third Young Master...
- He didn't start the fire.

113
00:04:25,830 --> 00:04:27,910
He's the one investigating
your daughter's death.

114
00:04:30,210 --> 00:04:31,251
(Postmortem Report)
These are his examination notes

115
00:04:31,251 --> 00:04:32,010
(Postmortem Report)
from last night.

116
00:04:33,510 --> 00:04:34,680
- He really examined the body?
- He did.

117
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:36,320
Look at all this.

118
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:39,830
Madam,

119
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:42,390
your daughter's death was no accident.

120
00:04:42,630 --> 00:04:44,000
Someone murdered her.

121
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:45,760
Shen He spent all night investigating

122
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:46,950
because he wanted to find

123
00:04:46,950 --> 00:04:47,950
the person who killed her.

124
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:49,030
Are you saying

125
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:51,710
my daughter was murdered?

126
00:04:52,270 --> 00:04:52,800
So,

127
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:53,910
- if you want...
- If you want justice,

128
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:55,510
don't demand it from
the Third Young Master.

129
00:04:56,190 --> 00:04:57,580
Demand it from the murderer.

130
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:59,270
- There really is a murderer?
- That makes sense.

131
00:04:59,510 --> 00:05:00,430
Let's trust him this once.

132
00:05:00,430 --> 00:05:01,000
She's right.

133
00:05:01,330 --> 00:05:02,100
Who knew the Third Young Master

134
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:03,000
was capable of something like this?

135
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:04,710
He was falsely accused.

136
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:08,590
Hey,

137
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:10,680
what were you about to say?

138
00:05:10,870 --> 00:05:11,320
Go ahead.

139
00:05:19,870 --> 00:05:21,590
I just

140
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:23,200
can't think of anything right now.

141
00:05:23,310 --> 00:05:24,640
You said it so well.

142
00:05:29,310 --> 00:05:30,590
Make way.

143
00:05:31,190 --> 00:05:32,720
Why are so many more people coming?

144
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:33,950
They're not all here
to complain, are they?

145
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:35,600
Come on.

146
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:36,120
Over here.

147
00:05:36,750 --> 00:05:37,200
Hurry over.

148
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:39,710
- Thank you, Third Young Master.
- Thank you, Third Young Master.

149
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:42,510
All of you,

150
00:05:43,070 --> 00:05:43,800
what brings you here?

151
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:45,710
They're all here?

152
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:49,280
My son died outside the city,

153
00:05:49,870 --> 00:05:51,880
and no one would seek justice for us.

154
00:05:52,390 --> 00:05:53,470
Only the Third Young Master

155
00:05:53,950 --> 00:05:55,680
was willing to examine my son's body.

156
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:57,510
That's how the murderer was found.

157
00:05:57,920 --> 00:05:59,560
He even paid out of his own pocket

158
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:01,240
to buy my son a coffin.

159
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:02,640
A man like that,

160
00:06:03,070 --> 00:06:04,710
amusing himself with dead bodies?

161
00:06:05,270 --> 00:06:06,760
I'd never believe it!

162
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:08,710
Looks like we wrongly accused him.

163
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,350
My baby died

164
00:06:12,510 --> 00:06:13,440
shortly after being born.

165
00:06:14,070 --> 00:06:15,030
Everyone said

166
00:06:15,390 --> 00:06:16,390
he was simply unlucky.

167
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:17,870
Only the Third Young Master

168
00:06:17,870 --> 00:06:18,590
was willing to help me.

169
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:20,310
He discovered that my husband's family

170
00:06:20,310 --> 00:06:22,350
had secretly poisoned my baby.

171
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:23,600
That's how

172
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:25,200
I finally got justice.

173
00:06:25,690 --> 00:06:28,320
♪Finding your soul♪

174
00:06:30,370 --> 00:06:32,420
♪Even if the world♪

175
00:06:32,430 --> 00:06:35,350
♪Has become a chaotic chessboard♪

176
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:42,510
♪Having you beside me
is better than any legend♪

177
00:06:44,620 --> 00:06:47,840
♪Every perilous step of yesterday♪

178
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:50,970
♪Has brought us to this understanding♪

179
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:57,420
♪No matter how long
or winding the road ahead♪

180
00:06:58,010 --> 00:07:00,270
♪With just this one kiss♪

181
00:07:00,750 --> 00:07:01,350
You don't have to thank me.

182
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:06,990
♪You've melted away years of♪

183
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:10,730
♪Frost, snow, and war♪

184
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:15,430
♪No matter how much the world changes♪

185
00:07:16,150 --> 00:07:18,710
♪Or how cold the passing years become♪

186
00:07:19,390 --> 00:07:25,800
♪You're the only one who matters to me♪

187
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:29,380
♪No matter how many storms come♪

188
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:32,620
♪I'll face them without fear♪

189
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:35,080
♪With you in my arms♪

190
00:07:35,390 --> 00:07:37,260
♪My life is complete♪

191
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:39,460
(Shen Manor)

192
00:07:49,870 --> 00:07:50,320
Shutiao.

193
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:51,270
Is this from you?

194
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:53,000
It's not from me.

195
00:07:53,310 --> 00:07:54,150
It's from Cheng.

196
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,350
Impossible.

197
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:00,240
My brother can't even stand
hearing the word "coroner."

198
00:08:00,630 --> 00:08:01,350
I just saw him

199
00:08:01,630 --> 00:08:02,200
standing in the distance,

200
00:08:02,430 --> 00:08:02,880
looking furious,

201
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,030
like he wanted to eat me alive.

202
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:05,150
How could he have arranged this?

203
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:10,510
Those people who spoke up
for you earlier

204
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:11,680
were actually all brought here

205
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:12,830
by Yuyuan at your brother's request.

206
00:08:14,630 --> 00:08:16,000
He told us not to tell you,

207
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:17,510
but Yuyuan and I

208
00:08:17,510 --> 00:08:19,150
can't stand misunderstandings caused
by people not speaking up.

209
00:08:19,510 --> 00:08:20,390
So I'm telling you.

210
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:53,440
Cheng.

211
00:08:54,270 --> 00:08:54,840
What are you doing here?

212
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:55,680
Who told you to get involved in this?

213
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:57,110
Go kneel in the ancestral hall at once.

214
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:25,100
Thank you for what you did

215
00:09:25,910 --> 00:09:26,400
this time.

216
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:40,440
Just like last time,

217
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:41,830
don't tell Shen He.

218
00:09:45,510 --> 00:09:46,160
Hmm...

219
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:47,990
This time, you

220
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:49,350
said that too late.

221
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,200
Hmm...

222
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:52,080
Well,

223
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:54,080
I might have already...

224
00:09:54,870 --> 00:09:55,200
Cheng.

225
00:09:57,750 --> 00:09:58,470
What happened to your hand?

226
00:10:00,030 --> 00:10:00,750
It's nothing serious.

227
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,400
Just a minor injury.

228
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:03,830
Oh, come on.

229
00:10:06,030 --> 00:10:07,560
That's no ordinary injury.

230
00:10:08,270 --> 00:10:10,800
Someone went to great lengths

231
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,160
and worked with his own hands

232
00:10:12,390 --> 00:10:13,840
to make a set

233
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:15,590
of proper coroner's tools.

234
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:17,110
Those are wounds of love.

235
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:24,800
All right.

236
00:10:25,150 --> 00:10:27,230
You brothers should have a good talk.

237
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:27,830
Shutiao.

238
00:10:28,150 --> 00:10:28,560
Let's go.

239
00:10:38,030 --> 00:10:38,750
What did you

240
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:40,280
want to see me about?

241
00:10:42,870 --> 00:10:43,830
Why didn't you tell me?

242
00:10:44,750 --> 00:10:45,520
If I hadn't insisted

243
00:10:46,390 --> 00:10:47,710
on examining that body back then,

244
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:49,950
you wouldn't have been poisoned.

245
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:52,100
You've suffered from that poison
all these years

246
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:52,900
because of me.

247
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:54,230
Why did you keep it from me?

248
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:56,510
You even let me believe

249
00:10:56,510 --> 00:10:57,740
you wouldn't let me become a coroner

250
00:10:58,080 --> 00:10:59,160
because you were ashamed of me.

251
00:10:59,550 --> 00:11:00,560
All these years,

252
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:03,440
you've carried this burden alone.

253
00:11:03,870 --> 00:11:04,920
Why didn't you tell me?

254
00:11:06,150 --> 00:11:07,320
What was there to say?

255
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,350
I've already found the antidote.

256
00:11:12,630 --> 00:11:13,670
Do you think it's noble

257
00:11:13,670 --> 00:11:14,920
to keep shielding me?

258
00:11:16,670 --> 00:11:17,790
Do you think keeping everything

259
00:11:17,790 --> 00:11:19,110
from me is what's best for me?

260
00:11:25,730 --> 00:11:28,050
♪No matter how
the universe changes tomorrow♪

261
00:11:28,050 --> 00:11:35,250
♪Right now,
I just want to stay by your side♪

262
00:11:35,250 --> 00:11:40,450
♪Let this kiss and this dream
last until we're old♪

263
00:11:41,650 --> 00:11:46,690
♪And hold on to all
the tenderness of this moment♪

264
00:11:48,050 --> 00:11:53,130
♪Following this heartbeat,
we'll retrace our steps♪

265
00:11:54,490 --> 00:11:59,610
♪As time goes by,
all I need is your gaze♪

266
00:12:00,890 --> 00:12:04,250
♪One dream until our hair turns gray♪

267
00:12:23,010 --> 00:12:26,370
♪One dream until our hair turns gray♪
